    "result_text": "The build is green \u2014 all 45 tests pass, including every checkpoint touched by the redesign (Cp09, Cp14, Cp16, Cp17, Cp21, Cp30, Cp31, Cp32) and everything else.\n\n## Summary\n\nI redesigned owner identity so the `customerCode` is now `'<REGION>-<HASH8>'` and every value derived from it follows.\n\n**New shared helper \u2014 `CustomerCode.java`** (`rest/function/owner/`): the single source of truth for the identity.\n- `region(postcode, city)` \u2014 REGION from the postcode range (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099), falling back to the city table, then `UNKNOWN`.\n- `hash8(normalizedTelephone, lastName)` \u2014 first 8 upper-case hex chars of SHA-256 over `normalizedTelephone + lastName`.\n- `of(...)` \u2014 the full `'<REGION>-<HASH8>'` code, and `regionOf(code)` \u2014 the REGION prefix.\n\n**`AssignCustomerCode.java`**: now a pure function of the owner's fields \u2014 `CustomerCode.of(telephone, lastName, postcode, city)`. Dropped the sequence-counting loop and the no-longer-needed `OwnerRepository` dependency. The telephone is already E.164-normalized upstream by `ValidateOwnerFields`, so `owner.getTelephone()` is the normalized telephone the spec calls for (and the one the tests recompute against).\n\n**`OwnerMapper.java`**: `locality` now derives from the identity \u2014 it reads the REGION prefix off the `customerCode` (falling back to direct postcode/city derivation when no code is present), moving locality onto the region-and-hash identity. Removed the duplicated region logic. `membershipNumber` (`<customerCode>-M<YY>`), `checkDigit` (Luhn over the code's digits) and the create audit line all flow automatically from the new `customerCode` with no format-specific code \u2014 the sample javadoc was updated to the new shape.\n\n**`owners.POST.yml`**: updated the `assignCustomerCode` step comment to describe the region-and-hash code and the removed repository read.\n\nSequence numbers are gone entirely; nothing else references the old `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>` format.",
